Suppose first that $r<R_0$. Apply Lemma~\ref{lem:small} at this
same $k$. Its tail bound gives
\[
 \Prob\{\norm{G-I_r}>\varepsilon\}
 \le\frac{r(r+1)}{k\varepsilon^2}
 \le\frac{r+1}{C}
 \le\frac{2R_0}{200R_0}=0.01.
\]
Here $r+1\le2R_0$ and $C\ge200R_0$ suffice; the estimate holds
at the prescribed width without any further choice of sample size.

